g major threats to global health over the remainder of the century. We argue that recent global shocks (including COVID-19, Ebola Bundibugyo virus disease, major geopolitical conflict, accelerating climate impacts, rapid shifts in development assistance, and the emergence of powerful artificial intelligence [AI] systems) show how quickly assumptions about stability can be overturned—and why governments and multilateral institutions must counter short-termism and localism with systematic, repeatable risk assessment and preparedness planning.","display_url":"thelancet.com/journals/lance…","end":164,"expanded_url":"https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(26)01714-9/fulltext","images":[{"height":202,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109136986623840256/17Qbo0pE?format=jpg&name=orig","width":739},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109136986623840256/17Qbo0pE?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":141,"status":200,"title":"The Lancet Commission on 21st century global threats to health","unwound_url":"https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(26)01714-9/abstract","url":"https://t.co/xr4oKEHujR"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/SpYyjzmHUV","end":197,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2109428848748302483/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109428184919969792","start":174,"url":"https://t.co/SpYyjzmHUV"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/SpYyjzmHUV","end":197,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2109428848748302483/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109428225906737153","start":174,"url":"https://t.co/SpYyjzmHUV"}]},"id":"2109428848748302483","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":371,"impression_count":64876,"like_count":795,"quote_count":22,"reply_count":38,"retweet_count":351},"text":"Just published @TheLancet \nGlobal threats to health in the 21st century\nan opus, 59 page comprehensive dissection of all the threats we face\nhttps://t.co/xr4oKEHujR @IHME_UW https://t.co/SpYyjzmHUV","url":"https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2109428848748302483"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109396121889968128"]},"author_id":"860158302","created_at":"2026-10-11T21:30:01.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109396124679242016"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/ZDi8omkmd2","end":296,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2109396124679242016/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109396121889968128","start":273,"url":"https://t.co/ZDi8omkmd2"}]},"id":"2109396124679242016","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":2,"impression_count":8097,"like_count":40,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":3,"retweet_count":4},"text":"Researchers traverse across Antarctica in minus 50 degree wind chill to validate measurements from NASA’s Ice, Cloud and Land Elevation Satellite. “Cold, dry air fills your nose and lungs. Your eyes blink, trying in vain to bat away the overwhelming brilliance of sunlight https://t.co/ZDi8omkmd2","url":"https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2109396124679242016"},{"author_id":"860158302","created_at":"2026-10-11T21:19:00.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109393354408505518"],"entities":{"urls":[{"description":"In the shadow of a rumored AI proof of one of the biggest problems in their field, three computer scientists rushed to publish their own milestone result.","display_url":"quantamagazine.org/as-ai-closed-i…","end":234,"expanded_url":"https://www.quantamagazine.org/as-ai-closed-in-on-unique-games-proof-researchers-raced-to-beat-the-machines-20261007/","images":[{"height":630,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2107853888262950912/0qTNhivg?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1200},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2107853888262950912/0qTNhivg?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":211,"status":200,"title":"As AI Closed In on ‘Unique Games’ Proof, Researchers Raced to Beat the Machines | Quanta Magazine","unwound_url":"https://www.quantamagazine.org/as-ai-closed-in-on-unique-games-proof-researchers-raced-to-beat-the-machines-20261007/","url":"https://t.co/Ql8xZlVMre"}]},"id":"2109393354408505518","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":35,"impression_count":8823,"like_count":78,"quote_count":2,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":8},"text":"A new breakthrough result in computational complexity theory concerns a class of problems that crop up in everyday life: filling in a sudoku puzzle, for instance, or planning seating arrangements for a wedding.\nhttps://t.co/Ql8xZlVMre","url":"https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2109393354408505518"},{"author_id":"860158302","created_at":"2026-10-11T21:18:00.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109393102490284287"],"entities":{"urls":[{"description":"C.H. Waddington’s powerful image of embryonic stem cells specializing on a rolling landscape has captivated biologists since the 1950s. Experimental data is finally confirming, and complicating, his visionary ideas.","display_url":"quantamagazine.org/how-does-life-…","end":146,"expanded_url":"https://www.quantamagazine.org/how-does-life-unfold-a-landscape-metaphor-comes-into-its-own-20261009/","images":[{"height":630,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2108559657027747840/vNXCVlAT?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1200},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2108559657027747840/vNXCVlAT?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":123,"status":200,"title":"How Does Life Unfold? A Landscape Metaphor Comes Into Its Own. | Quanta Magazine","unwound_url":"https://www.quantamagazine.org/how-does-life-unfold-a-landscape-metaphor-comes-into-its-own-20261009/","url":"https://t.co/MjiZa14iSq"}]},"id":"2109393102490284287","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":34,"impression_count":10727,"like_count":83,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":14},"text":"What processes ensure that a liver cell will stay a liver cell as it progresses through an organism’s development process?\nhttps://t.co/MjiZa14iSq","url":"https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2109393102490284287"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109382386815528960"]},"author_id":"86626845","created_at":"2026-10-11T20:41:31.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109383921083506902"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":269,"id":"296644509","start":259,"username":"JShendure"}],"urls":[{"description":"Mammalian biology unfolds over time, within tissues and organs opaque to our eyes and instruments. We applied DNA Typewriter, a sequential molecular recorder, to record the cell lineage of a mouse over nearly two weeks of development. From one embryo, we ...","display_url":"science.org/doi/10.1126/sc…","end":258,"expanded_url":"https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.ael0508?referrer=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nature.com%2F","images":[{"height":550,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109383924531302400/0pBT5WoH?format=jpg&name=orig","width":715},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109383924531302400/0pBT5WoH?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":235,"status":200,"title":"A DNA Typewriter records the cell lineage history of a mouse, from zygote to late organogenesis","unwound_url":"https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.ael0508?referrer=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nature.com%2F","url":"https://t.co/tyrgVzzHA8"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/eEbQ1OhWuu","end":293,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2109383921083506902/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109382386815528960","start":270,"url":"https://t.co/eEbQ1OhWuu"}]},"id":"2109383921083506902","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":107,"impression_count":30742,"like_count":286,"quote_count":9,"reply_count":11,"retweet_count":69},"text":"When genome editing got going, the ability to trace a mammalian embryo's development to organ generation in exquisite detail was not envisioned. Now it's been accomplished by 2 independent groups. A big week in  developmental biology \nhttps://t.co/tyrgVzzHA8 @JShendure https://t.co/eEbQ1OhWuu","url":"https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2109383921083506902"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109357572985864192"]},"author_id":"86626845","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:59:14.000Z","edit_histo